<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0490e6d5dfc4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber CEO Dara Khosrowshahi also tweeted his condolences on Monday morning," ;
    airo:sourceDocId "562" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/068363d104fb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A self-driving Uber car killed a pedestrian in Arizona on Sunday evening." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "183" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0a1a0f5eb25c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A dashboard camera video of the incident, captured by a Luxor Cab taxi, shows a self-driving Volvo SUV zooming through the light long after it turned red and coming uncomfortably close to a pedestrian." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "561" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0a5270e65fc5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The report said police concluded the crash, which has dealt Uber Technologies Inc a major setback in its efforts to develop self-driving cars, would have been “entirely avoidable” if Vasquez had been paying attention." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0adc7f92f3e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Arizona Gov. Doug Duccey said earlier this week he's suspending Uber's ability to test self-driving cars on the state's roads, saying he found video of the deadly collision \"disturbing and alarming.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "560" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0f119dc937ca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tempe Police have released new body camera video and the police report from the night of March 19, when a self-driving Uber hit and killed a pedestrian mid-block on Mill Avenue.",
        "Tempe Police have released new body camera video and the police report from the night of March 19." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1a7a6b2cce6a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber car's 'safety' driver streamed TV show before fatal crash: police" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e952e685f4e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla Motors was the first to disclose a death involving a self-driving car in 2016 when the sensors of a Model S driving in autopilot mode failed to detect a large white 18-wheel truck and trailer crossing the highway." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e9a9ad29f53> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Elon Musk, Tesla’s CEO, said, “I think in the next year, self-driving will encompass essentially all modes of driving.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "183" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/217f59081ebb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Multiple experts have raised questions about Uber’s Lidar technology, which is the system of lasers that the autonomous cars uses to “see” the world around them." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1079" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2813b22baa43> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The driver behind the wheel of an autonomous Uber vehicle that fatally struck a woman in Tempe in March was watching 'The Voice' via a streaming service in the minutes leading up to the crash, a police report says." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29ec2e49ef77> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Facial recognition was one of the key capabilities that it boasted, but it was found to have a weakness for identical twins." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a880860d802> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber Driver in Fatal Tempe Crash May Have Been Watching The Voice Behind the Wheel" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2c0747667da3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Tempe police are working with Uber representatives, the National Transportation Safety Board and the US Department of Transportation's National Highway Traffic Safety Administration in their investigation to determine who, or what, was at fault for the accident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "560" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/30b1111c8a2f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "That's not all, a week after the phone's release, Vietnamese security firm Bkav, using a mask with 3D printed base, convinced the phone that it was human and made the phone to unlock itself." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

