<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0d5be4986ae1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In May, the National Transportation Safety Board determined Uber's self-driving car accurately identified Herzberg, but Uber had turned off the vehicle's automatic emergency braking, so the SUV did not attempt to brake." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "565" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/25467b3f6407> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber’s spokesperson said that the company is reviewing safety practices and procedures and has hired former National Transportation Safety Board chair Christopher Hart as a safety advisor." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/304ac4ccb355> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "police obtained a search warrant for Vasquez's two cellphones and served warrants on three companies that provide streaming services — Hulu, Netflix and Google, which owns YouTube — in an effort to determine if the driver had been watching shows on her phones while driving." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3219b2364c30> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[452] In a tragic incident involving Uber self driving car, a woman was killed during a trial, stalling autonomous vehicle operations worldwide." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/53064fdee96b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "She drove a gray Volvo SUV, rigged up with cameras and lidar sensors." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5e0546c4a194> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The backup \"safety driver\" in an Uber Technologies self-driving vehicle that killed a pedestrian in March was streaming the popular television show The Voice on her mobile phone in the moments before the crash, according to police in Arizona." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5e1bdb4e6d06> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "So Uber poached 40 experts from Carnegie Mellon’s robotics department to create something called the Uber Advanced Technologies Group and tasked it with turning the company into a self‑driving force.",
        "So Uber poached 40 experts from Carnegie Mellon’s robotics department to create something called the Uber Advanced Technologies Group." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/607a3922b2aa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber has said it's in the middle of a top-to-bottom review of its safety culture, including operating procedures for its vehicle operators, led by former National Transportation Safety Board Chairman Christopher Hart." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5042" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/674daf23884b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The case has now been handed over to the Yavapai County Attorney for review of possible charges against the backup driver, Rafaela Vasquez." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/714163d82045> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[554] Back in March, an Uber self-driving car killed 49-year-old Elain Herzberg in Tempe, Arizona, after failing to do an emergency stop." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/718426a59b15> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In August, Ducey signed an exuberant executive order allowing companies to test self-driving vehicles on public roads." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8596bec357b6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "3. When Autonomous And Driverless Vehicles Turned Disastrous" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9a0e2c6b6b16> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Uber car, a Volvo XC90 sport utility vehicle outfitted with the company’s sensing system, was in autonomous mode with a human safety driver at the wheel but carrying no passengers when it struck Elaine Herzberg, a 49-year-old woman, on Sunday around 10 p.m." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8676bfe0f03> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "At 1 point, a Ducey staffer emailed Uber and referred to a 2015 Arizona law that regulated ride-sharing as “your bill.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b4662fd51428> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A 49-year-old woman was hit and killed by a self-driving Volvo operated by Uber while crossing a street in Tempe." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bf78bf081a42> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Using an executive order, Mr. Ducey opened the state to testing of autonomous vehicles that had safety drivers at the wheel, ready to take over in an emergency." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c8b3755da3b6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[183] A self-driving Uber car killed a pedestrian in Arizona on Sunday evening." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "183" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ef724c70921c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Senate bill, if passed, would free autonomous-car makers from some existing safety standards and pre-empt states from creating their own vehicle safety laws." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

