<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/014fb26dd467> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the NTSB’s preliminary report on the incident, Uber’s self-driving car was able to detect Herzberg as she was attempting to cross the road but failed to brake.",
        "According to the NTSB’s preliminary report on the incident, Uber’s self-driving car was able to detect Herzberg as she was attempting to cross the road but failed to brake. Per that report, the car’s radar and LIDAR sensors were able to detect an object in the path of the vehicle — Herzberg — about six seconds before the crash, but it misclassified her as an unknown object, then a vehicle, then finally a bicycle." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "553" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2792a0f79ffd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Face ID, a face mapping technology that can unlock phones, verify Apple Pay and replace fingerprint scanners, could be fooled at some level, especially when identical twins are made to use the Face ID." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2eec0f172d92> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The 2017 Volvo SUV was traveling at roughly 40 miles an hour, and it did not appear that the car slowed down as it approached the woman, said Tempe sergeant Ronald Elcock." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3a365f0b87ec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Back in March, an Uber self-driving car killed 49-year-old Elain Herzberg in Tempe, Arizona, after failing to do an emergency stop." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4136aba602cd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "At the time, its CEO, Travis Kalanick, saw the development of robotaxis as an existential battle, particularly with Google." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1353" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6be8b610c386> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Bryan Reimer, director of the Advanced Technology Vehicle (ATV) Consortium at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5042" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6e8dd1376981> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The crash of an Uber self-driving car that killed an Arizona woman in March was “entirely avoidable,” according to police reports released by the Tempe Police Department." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/72e723d7a896> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Details from the police report were published Thursday by the Arizona Republic, Reuters, and other media outlets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5042" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7e58ffc58fcb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "She flipped the Volvo into autonomous mode, and the car navigated itself through a blur of suburban Arizona." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8747a3fa60ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber’s autonomous technology failed to detect Herzberg, and the human driver who was supposed to act as a safeguard appeared distracted in previously released footage." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9d25edc954b3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We have in the past seen instances such as the failure of Microsoft bot Tay, when it developed a tendency to come up with racist remarks." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c0807c6c3e0c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The computer-vision systems in self-driving cars are trained to identify things, such as other vehicles, trees, sign posts, bicycles, and so on, and make decisions on what to do next using that information." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1190" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cc4691687610> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“This is exactly the type of situation that Lidar and radar are supposed to pick up,” said David King, an Arizona State University professor and transportation planning expert." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1079" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d0222d91480a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This week, the Massachusetts Department of Transportation and 14 cities in the state agreed to allow testing of autonomous vehicles if companies enter into a memorandum of understanding, promising that their testing has been safe and \"further testing of AVs is reasonably expected to be conducted safely and efficiently.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5042" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ed475d86c55f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As scary as it may sound, “Bob” and “Alice”, the chatbots created by Facebook had to be shut down as the duo started communicating in their own language, defying human generated algorithms." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0368d034a22d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber is cooperating with the Tempe police investigation, the company told Quartz." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1188" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/108c40b8b379> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The operator was not looking at the road the moments before the car hit 49-year-old Elaine Herzberg at around 40 mph." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/15eda6d953bb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Business-­boosting governor Doug Ducey, the former CEO of Cold Stone Creamery, took office in 2015." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1eeb9c29ba22> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Uber driving system—which had been in full control of the car for 19 minutes at that point—registered a vehicle ahead that was 5.6 seconds away, but it delivered no alert to Vasquez.",
        "The Uber driving system—which had been in full control of the car for 19 minutes at that point—registered a vehicle ahead that was 5.6 seconds away." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2339edd585fb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "John Simpson, the privacy and technology project director with Consumer Watchdog, said the video revealed a “complete failure” of Uber’s technology and its safety protocols." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1079" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3583ec1e54f5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the gray Volvo, operated by Uber, hit her at about 40 mph" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "561" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/41f8c7627c76> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After a US federal investigation, it is thought that the car did not stop because the system put in place to carry out emergency stops in dangerous situations was disabled ." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/52af65e4f07e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police also sent search warrants to YouTube, Netflix, and Hulu to recover Vasquez’s viewing history on her devices around the time of the accident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "564" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/57af2c8f3981> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Maricopa County Attorney's Office was originally given the case, but handed it over to Yavapai because of a \"conflict of interest.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "563" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/735b642964ff> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police in Tempe, Arizona, have released a new report regarding Uber’s fatal self-driving car crash last March, which reveals that the safety driver Rafaela Vasquez was streaming The Voice on Hulu on her phone at the time of the accident, via Reuters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "553" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a1eed969aa70> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On-board video footage showed the victim, 49-year-old Elaine Herzberg, pushing her bike at night across a road in Tempe, Arizona, moments before she was struck by the AI-powered SUV at 39 MPH." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1190" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a799a5f9310b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A spokesperson for Arizona governor Doug Ducey says, ‘We await the more thorough and final investigative report. Uber’s self-driving vehicle suspension remains in place.’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b65aa8228361> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, 37,461 people died in traffic-related accidents in the United States, according to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bba629f2fb14> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Police have emphasized that the victim was not in a crosswalk at the time of the crash, but experts said the technology still should have stopped the vehicle, a Volvo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1079" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d423e2a5642a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "That's according to an official dossier published by the US National Safety Transportation Board (NTSB) on Tuesday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1190" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d5a39b71e0fa> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Her stream ended at 9.59pm, around the same time Elaine Herzberg, 49, was hit by the Uber, which was in self-driving mode, the report said." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d71e15499987> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The NTSB, or National Transportation Safety Board, has launched an investigation into yesterday’s fatality." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "183" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/df28d4e00a94> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Uber’s self-driving Volvo SUV was traveling at just under 44 miles (71 km) per hour." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e7dbf6df6ca8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In California, where testing without a backup driver was just weeks away from being permitted, Jessica Gonzalez, a spokeswoman for the state Department of Motor Vehicles, said officials were in the process of gathering more information about the Tempe crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fa25509aa18c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Business-­boosting governor Doug Ducey, the former CEO of Cold Stone Creamery, took office in 2015, promising to yank the state out of its post-­recession doldrums." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1353" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/16af0f1f9c9c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Days after a self-driving Uber SUV struck a 49-year-old pedestrian while she was crossing the street with her bicycle in Tempe, Arizona, footage released by police revealed that the vehicle was moving in autonomous mode." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1079" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2a1fe9f7c080> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "John M Simpson, privacy and technology project director with Consumer Watchdog, said the collision highlighted the need for tighter regulations of the nascent technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3900fef18563> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Maricopa County Attorney's Office was last reported to have referred the case to the Yavapai County Attorney's Office." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/70f889f3cf9b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "said David Friedman, director of cars for Consumers Union, which is the advocacy division of Consumer Reports." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "561" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9e59d6b0140e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Tempe police are working with Uber representatives, the National Transportation Safety Board and the US Department of Transportation's National Highway Traffic Safety Administration in their investigation to determine who, or what, was at fault for the accident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "560" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a022d5e9b3b9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Maricopa County Attorney's Office referred the case to the Yavapai County Attorney's office because of a conflict and that office could not be reached late Thursday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "555" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/abf5b3dd4ea6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A report by the Tempe Police Department said the driver, Rafaela Vasquez, repeatedly looked down and not at the road, glancing up a half second before the car hit Elaine Herzberg, 49, who was crossing the street at night." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "556" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c19c3bcf9a89> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meanwhile, the Tempe police are working with Uber representatives, the NTSB and the US Department of Transportation's National Highway Traffic Safety Administration in their investigation to determine who, or what, was at fault for the accident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "559" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/14f5993918e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "there have been at least three crashes involving Teslas in autopilot mode, one of which was fatal." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "562" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/89ca2024df50> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla Motors was the first to disclose a death involving a self-driving car in 2016 when the sensors of a Model S driving in autopilot mode failed to detect a large white 18-wheel truck and trailer crossing the highway." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "568" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c6e207e79557> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Waymo made a decision early in its testing program to aim first for full automation in its software after its trained employees couldn't stay focused on the road as the cars drove themselves." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5042" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dac0933764ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The popular Amazon Echo cost one of its owners a huge locksmith bill, when police had to break down the house on complaints from neighbours of loud music early in the morning." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/82a04208f616> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, with Google’s Waymo and GM’s Cruise already piloting prototype self-driving cars around the Phoenix area." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5046" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8333b131fa1e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "When Apple released its iPhone X with much aplomb, it was awed for its artificial intelligence and machine learning capabilities." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/46067778642c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla is 1 of the most “exposed” companies to the self-driving initiative, and it has been vocal about providing Level 5 autonomous driving or completely hands free under all conditions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "183" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/799eeac74fd8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A 318-page report filed by the Tempe Police Department refutes driver Rafaela Vasquez's previous statement to federal safety investigators that she wasn't using her mobile devices when the car struck and killed a woman who was crossing the street at night." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "558" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0e243e9a169a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Whilst regulators continue to investigate the cause of the crash, Uber has suspended tests on their self-driving cars in San Francisco, Toronto, Arizona, and Pittsburgh." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "554" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/829a20ee4600> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In the wake of the crash, Uber has now suspended all its self-driving car tests in the city, as well as in the Bay Area, Pittsburgh, and Toronto, according to The Wall Street Journal (paywall)." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1188" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/96be890c5612> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, a man driving his Tesla using Autopilot, the car company’s self-driving feature, died on a state highway in Florida when his car crashed into a tractor-trailer that was crossing the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/76b6df9c2fe6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A self-driving Uber car killed a pedestrian in Arizona on Sunday evening." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "183" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c36949e6c626> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Waymo, the self-driving car unit of Google’s parent company Alphabet, has been using cars without a human in the driver’s seat to pick up and drop off passengers in Arizona." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2806b3a3bf5c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Waymo, Lyft and Cruise, an autonomous vehicle company owned by General Motors, did not respond to requests for comment." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1191" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b38f8913d12d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The indigenously built robot called Mitra, developed by Bengaluru-based Invento Robotics walked up to welcome Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Ivanka Trump at the the Global Entrepreneurship Summit (GES) opening in Hyderabad." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "452" .

